1
00:00:57,641 --> 00:00:59,226
You evil cat.

2
00:01:04,023 --> 00:01:05,608
You're just like Yoon Yi-jun!

3
00:01:21,165 --> 00:01:22,500
You little brat!

4
00:01:30,716 --> 00:01:34,178
What kind of drunk behavior is that?

5
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:35,387
Whatever.

6
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:41,602
What if he gets hurt?

7
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:44,063
Who's going to take care of me?

8
00:01:51,028 --> 00:01:52,321
Who told him to get drunk?

9
00:01:56,909 --> 00:01:58,661
What's going on?

10
00:02:08,379 --> 00:02:10,130
Special Forces! You!

11
00:02:11,006 --> 00:02:12,299
Move!

12
00:02:15,094 --> 00:02:16,220
I'm dizzy.

13
00:02:23,269 --> 00:02:24,186
Come here!

14
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:50,004
Who hits someone and just walks off?

15
00:03:27,082 --> 00:03:29,460
You little punk.

16
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:41,305
Special Forces, why don't you get up?

17
00:03:41,388 --> 00:03:45,184
I need to talk to you
about something urgent.

18
00:03:52,316 --> 00:03:53,359
Special Forces.

19
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:55,903
Special Forces.

20
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:58,697
Do you really want to get fired?

21
00:04:12,211 --> 00:04:13,379
You're noisy.

22
00:04:46,412 --> 00:04:47,579
Hey.

23
00:04:50,958 --> 00:04:52,459
I said wake up.

24
00:04:54,086 --> 00:04:55,170
What?

25
00:04:56,755 --> 00:04:57,756
What?

26
00:04:59,008 --> 00:05:00,259
Don't…

27
00:05:28,412 --> 00:05:30,497
EPISODE 5

28
00:05:54,938 --> 00:05:56,732
BASED ON "WHY DON'T YOU KNOW I'M A WOMAN?"

29
00:05:56,815 --> 00:05:57,733
What are you doing?

30
00:05:58,233 --> 00:05:59,193
Why are you here?

31
00:05:59,276 --> 00:06:01,111
-This is my house.
-What?

32
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,740
Right. This is your house.

33
00:06:05,866 --> 00:06:08,619
So why am I here?

34
00:06:12,414 --> 00:06:14,917
Do you not remember anything?

35
00:06:17,377 --> 00:06:20,172
That could be a problem for you.

36
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:31,767
What? Whose clothes are these?

37
00:06:31,850 --> 00:06:33,435
What's all this?

38
00:06:33,519 --> 00:06:34,770
What's this?

39
00:06:36,146 --> 00:06:38,357
In any case, I'm so sorry!

40
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:39,942
I'm sorry, Mr. Yoon!

41
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:07,886
Excuse me, Mr. Yoon.

42
00:07:09,304 --> 00:07:10,389
I remember.

43
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,642
-Is that so? Then tell me.
-Yes.

44
00:07:14,226 --> 00:07:16,395
Firstly, though I refused multiple times,

45
00:07:16,478 --> 00:07:19,606
you adamantly took me
to that room on the second floor.

46
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,358
And?

47
00:07:21,984 --> 00:07:23,152
And…

48
00:07:23,652 --> 00:07:27,698
I officially apologized
for mistaking you for a perverted geek.

49
00:07:28,949 --> 00:07:29,908
And?

50
00:07:30,993 --> 00:07:33,620
And your ideal type.

51
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,959
Thank you for showing me.

52
00:07:41,879 --> 00:07:42,921
What else?

53
00:07:44,548 --> 00:07:45,382
What else?

54
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:48,844
Is there something else?

55
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:53,932
You don't remember.

56
00:07:54,433 --> 00:07:56,059
Otherwise, you wouldn't be like this.

57
00:07:56,143 --> 00:07:58,395
You should be on your knees
begging for forgiveness.

58
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:00,063
Did I make some kind of mistake?

59
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:01,732
Mistake?

60
00:08:01,815 --> 00:08:05,611
I was up all night,
and you don't even remember what you did?

61
00:08:05,694 --> 00:08:07,988
You stayed up all night because of me?

62
00:08:08,071 --> 00:08:09,531
-No.
-What?

63
00:08:11,867 --> 00:08:13,869
Yes, I did.

64
00:08:13,952 --> 00:08:15,996
But I didn't say it was because of you.

65
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:17,372
Yi-jun.

66
00:08:19,166 --> 00:08:20,584
You stayed up all night?

67
00:08:26,548 --> 00:08:27,633
It's been a while.

68
00:08:29,635 --> 00:08:30,844
My fiancé.

69
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:44,650
Captain, I figured it out.

70
00:08:45,275 --> 00:08:46,610
Yoon Yi-jun is…

71
00:08:46,693 --> 00:08:47,819
I have a bad feeling.

72
00:08:51,365 --> 00:08:52,699
Is this what I think it is?

73
00:08:58,372 --> 00:09:02,417
Maybe it's a type of code or signal.

74
00:09:03,418 --> 00:09:05,337
You know, like Morse code.

75
00:09:05,837 --> 00:09:07,631
"Captain, I figured it out."

76
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:09,549
"Yoon Yi-jun isn't this."

77
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:11,760
Are you serious?

78
00:09:11,843 --> 00:09:15,722
How is this Morse code?
This was clearly a text sent while drunk!

79
00:09:16,932 --> 00:09:19,601
You're right.
It's a text sent while drunk.

80
00:09:19,685 --> 00:09:21,687
She even promised not to drink.

81
00:09:21,770 --> 00:09:24,815
She's well aware of what happens
when she drinks, but she still drank!

82
00:09:25,732 --> 00:09:27,943
Don't take it out on me.
I'm not the one who drank.

83
00:09:28,026 --> 00:09:30,362
I need to teach you two a lesson.

84
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:31,738
Damn you.

85
00:09:32,823 --> 00:09:35,450
More importantly,
Yoon Yi-jun's fiancée is coming to Korea.

86
00:09:35,534 --> 00:09:37,661
-The director of Naon Art Center?
-Yes.

87
00:09:38,829 --> 00:09:41,415
Her grandpa's a party leader
and former Minister of Justice.

88
00:09:41,498 --> 00:09:44,126
A silver spoon whose dad
is a leading presidential candidate.

89
00:09:44,209 --> 00:09:46,586
-What, really?
-He's right.

90
00:09:47,254 --> 00:09:48,714
I told you so.

91
00:09:50,132 --> 00:09:51,091
Also,

92
00:09:51,967 --> 00:09:53,635
I heard a rumor about her.

93
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:56,763
-What is it?
-That woman

94
00:09:57,472 --> 00:09:58,807
is a bit strange.

95
00:10:06,648 --> 00:10:07,733
Bonjour.

96
00:10:08,775 --> 00:10:10,277
Nice to meet you.

97
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:12,779
Hello, ma'am.

98
00:10:13,697 --> 00:10:16,033
Stop bothering my secretary
and come sit down.

99
00:10:18,327 --> 00:10:20,662
When did you come back from Paris?

100
00:10:21,913 --> 00:10:24,291
I came back because I missed you.

101
00:10:24,374 --> 00:10:25,751
Don't be so creepy this early.

102
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:32,090
You're the cutest when you're grossed out.

103
00:10:32,799 --> 00:10:34,009
Did you two sleep together?

104
00:10:34,092 --> 00:10:35,344
-No.
-Are you crazy?

105
00:10:38,472 --> 00:10:39,348
How disappointing.

106
00:10:39,431 --> 00:10:41,516
I thought I had
stumbled on some spicy scene.

107
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,851
-No way.
-It's not like that.

108
00:10:45,062 --> 00:10:47,314
Then why are you in pajamas,

109
00:10:47,397 --> 00:10:50,650
and why is your secretary in your clothes?

110
00:10:51,485 --> 00:10:52,986
It's not what you think,

111
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:55,322
so mind your own business.

112
00:10:57,449 --> 00:11:00,410
Fine. I'll pretend nothing happened.

113
00:11:00,494 --> 00:11:01,995
-Nothing happened!
-It's nothing!

114
00:11:02,621 --> 00:11:04,164
-You, why…
-Sir, why…

115
00:11:04,247 --> 00:11:05,916
-Let me… I…
-Let me… Stop!

116
00:11:08,627 --> 00:11:10,087
Get ready for work and come back.

117
00:11:21,056 --> 00:11:24,059
Fine. You want me to leave
because your fiancée is here?

118
00:11:40,117 --> 00:11:40,951
Whatever.

119
00:11:48,083 --> 00:11:50,377
Do you want jealousy or indifference?

120
00:11:55,215 --> 00:11:56,341
I mean,

121
00:11:56,425 --> 00:11:58,385
secretaries and bosses flirt, date,

122
00:11:58,468 --> 00:12:00,554
even have affairs in dramas.

123
00:12:00,637 --> 00:12:02,139
He's a guy.

124
00:12:05,183 --> 00:12:07,894
You must be tired from the jet lag.

125
00:12:08,395 --> 00:12:10,397
Go sleep if you're going to talk nonsense.

126
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:14,401
How cruel. You let your secretary stay,
yet you kick out your fiancée?

127
00:12:15,902 --> 00:12:18,238
Now, that's really going
to make me jealous.

128
00:12:18,321 --> 00:12:20,282
Leave. I'm tired.

129
00:12:20,365 --> 00:12:23,160
-The shopping bags that I brought--
-Leave them.

130
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:26,746
Why would I? They're mine.

131
00:12:27,873 --> 00:12:30,542
I bought a couple of small things.

132
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:34,588
-Put it on expenses.
-Why would I?

133
00:12:34,671 --> 00:12:38,091
I turned off the CCTV camera
and even cleared the employee passage.

134
00:12:39,509 --> 00:12:41,970
I gave you a discount because we're close.

135
00:12:43,847 --> 00:12:45,390
I understand. You can leave now.

136
00:12:45,474 --> 00:12:46,892
By the way,

137
00:12:47,476 --> 00:12:49,436
did your tolerance go up,

138
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:51,688
or was it just a long night?

139
00:12:53,565 --> 00:12:56,276
Why is a foul-tempered guy like you
so worked up?

140
00:12:56,359 --> 00:13:00,447
Are you upset or lovestruck?

141
00:13:09,206 --> 00:13:10,665
I don't remember anything.

142
00:13:12,501 --> 00:13:15,754
What on earth did you do, Jae-hee?

143
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:19,925
Think. Think harder.

144
00:13:20,509 --> 00:13:23,261
Why do you only collect stuff like that?

145
00:13:24,930 --> 00:13:26,556
It's a little lousy.

146
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:28,600
Pervert. Geek.

147
00:13:29,184 --> 00:13:30,101
I drank.

148
00:13:30,185 --> 00:13:32,812
You stupid cat!

149
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:35,482
-Three!
-I was chasing the cat.

150
00:13:40,612 --> 00:13:41,696
I don't remember.

151
00:13:45,867 --> 00:13:46,701
No!

152
00:13:46,785 --> 00:13:47,869
Hey!

153
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,080
Just kidding.

154
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:51,414
Try to remember.

155
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:04,928
"Lovestruck"?

156
00:14:06,388 --> 00:14:07,722
"Upset"?

157
00:14:07,806 --> 00:14:09,808
I was just upset

158
00:14:10,392 --> 00:14:12,018
over my secretary's mistake.

159
00:14:16,815 --> 00:14:20,360
But how could he not remember it?

160
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,955
I need to pull it together.

161
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:44,509
MOBILE CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION TEAM 1

162
00:14:44,593 --> 00:14:45,760
WHAT HAPPENED, JAE-HEE?

163
00:14:45,844 --> 00:14:46,803
BONG-YI

164
00:14:50,765 --> 00:14:51,808
What do I do?

165
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,436
Solidarity.

166
00:14:54,519 --> 00:14:56,938
Solidarity, my foot.

167
00:14:57,022 --> 00:14:59,774
You said an order from a superior
is a matter of life and death.

168
00:14:59,858 --> 00:15:02,110
But our upright, military-minded
Detective Kang

169
00:15:02,193 --> 00:15:04,487
treated my words
like total crap last night.

170
00:15:04,571 --> 00:15:08,033
I had no choice. I'd already had a drink.

171
00:15:08,116 --> 00:15:09,868
What did you just say?

172
00:15:09,951 --> 00:15:12,579
What kind of a crappy excuse is that?

173
00:15:12,662 --> 00:15:15,582
And I didn't make any mistakes.

174
00:15:16,249 --> 00:15:17,626
I acted as usual,

175
00:15:18,585 --> 00:15:21,796
you know, running here and there.

176
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:23,590
You have the right to remain silent…

177
00:15:24,591 --> 00:15:27,677
Wait. Where are the handcuffs?

178
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:29,888
I must have lost them.

179
00:15:30,639 --> 00:15:31,681
This is crazy!

180
00:15:32,182 --> 00:15:34,976
What did you say, you punk?
Are you calling me crazy?

181
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:37,562
Are you going to go off the rails now?

182
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:40,482
I'm not going off the rails.

183
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:44,152
I wouldn't dare go against your orders
unless I were crazy.

184
00:15:44,235 --> 00:15:46,738
I only drank
because I had a clear purpose.

185
00:15:46,821 --> 00:15:49,115
And through my sacrifice,
I figured it out.

186
00:15:50,784 --> 00:15:51,826
Is that so?

187
00:15:52,827 --> 00:15:55,580
Then tell me what you figured out
through your sacrifice.

188
00:15:55,664 --> 00:15:58,875
Yoon Yi-jun didn't kill Han Eun-young.

189
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,460
It's his own statement.

190
00:16:00,543 --> 00:16:02,420
He actually feels guilty
toward the victim.

191
00:16:02,504 --> 00:16:04,923
-Hey, what do you mean?
-Are you sure?

192
00:16:06,424 --> 00:16:08,760
Yoon Yi-jun said that himself?

193
00:16:08,843 --> 00:16:11,388
Yes. He admitted it for the first time.

194
00:16:12,514 --> 00:16:16,226
The real killer is someone else.

195
00:16:16,685 --> 00:16:18,395
They used the chandelier and herbicide.

196
00:16:18,478 --> 00:16:20,146
They're clearly targeting Yoon Yi-jun.

197
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:22,273
Where the hell are they?

198
00:16:26,945 --> 00:16:28,697
Where is Captain Park?

199
00:16:32,701 --> 00:16:34,077
He asked to see you.

200
00:16:40,834 --> 00:16:41,668
Follow me.

201
00:16:42,836 --> 00:16:44,546
Let's go. Come on.

202
00:16:46,715 --> 00:16:47,549
Your phone.

203
00:16:50,218 --> 00:16:51,261
Watch out, Bong-yi.

204
00:16:51,886 --> 00:16:52,762
Never mind.

205
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:00,562
I feel bad for the captain.

206
00:17:01,271 --> 00:17:04,816
Should I go tell him
that Yoon Yi-jun is being threatened

207
00:17:04,899 --> 00:17:07,068
and someone else killed Secretary Han?

208
00:17:07,152 --> 00:17:08,361
Should I just report it?

209
00:17:08,445 --> 00:17:10,905
Are you also going to tell him
we went undercover?

210
00:17:10,989 --> 00:17:12,991
I'm just saying, out of frustration.

211
00:17:15,201 --> 00:17:17,370
I need to go work undercover.

212
00:17:17,912 --> 00:17:20,790
I'll look into the herbicide
as Detective Kang requested.

213
00:17:20,874 --> 00:17:21,916
Okay.

214
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:26,421
Hey, our captain will be fine, right?

215
00:17:26,504 --> 00:17:28,256
CHIEF'S OFFICE

216
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:29,257
A phone?

217
00:17:29,841 --> 00:17:32,469
What phone are you talking about?

218
00:17:37,849 --> 00:17:40,977
I heard about this
while settling with the family.

219
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,937
They told your team as well.

220
00:17:43,021 --> 00:17:46,524
Apparently, Han Eun-young had two phones.

221
00:17:47,692 --> 00:17:48,943
Why didn't you report it?

222
00:17:49,944 --> 00:17:52,155
Well, I recently found out.

223
00:17:53,531 --> 00:17:55,784
So are you searching for it or not?

224
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:59,454
We believe it disappeared from the scene.

225
00:18:00,497 --> 00:18:03,082
Are you sure? What's on the phone?

226
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:06,920
That's also what I am curious about.

227
00:18:08,171 --> 00:18:10,715
It's not like I can request a warrant
to search Taekang.

228
00:18:10,799 --> 00:18:12,300
-So--
-Come on!

229
00:18:12,383 --> 00:18:14,052
That's the situation.

230
00:18:14,135 --> 00:18:15,178
Detective.

231
00:18:17,013 --> 00:18:18,807
Where do you think the phone is?

232
00:18:28,024 --> 00:18:29,526
I'll let you handle it.

233
00:18:29,609 --> 00:18:30,693
Take care, ma'am.

234
00:18:37,408 --> 00:18:39,702
After Chairman Yoon withdrew
the succession plan,

235
00:18:39,786 --> 00:18:42,288
Yoon Na-jung immediately met Kim Si-hyun.

236
00:18:43,581 --> 00:18:45,124
The timing seems strange.

237
00:18:47,001 --> 00:18:51,506
The victim might have lost
the phone somewhere.

238
00:18:52,757 --> 00:18:53,925
Right.

239
00:18:55,677 --> 00:18:58,888
If you had known,
you would've already found the phone.

240
00:18:58,972 --> 00:19:00,181
Of course.

241
00:19:00,932 --> 00:19:02,725
It's difficult to be sure

242
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:05,270
if what the victim's family said
holds any water.

243
00:19:05,353 --> 00:19:08,439
But it's good to be sure.
Please find it as soon as you can.

244
00:19:09,357 --> 00:19:13,611
Like always, we'll provide any help
that we can.

245
00:19:13,695 --> 00:19:15,154
Of course, sir.

246
00:19:15,238 --> 00:19:18,449
We have to investigate fairly
and by the book.

247
00:19:18,533 --> 00:19:22,579
They're the detectives I saw
during the witness interview, right?

248
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:23,872
Special Investigation Team?

249
00:19:23,955 --> 00:19:27,834
You have quite a memory.
It must be because you're a lawyer.

250
00:19:27,917 --> 00:19:30,628
You've already seen two.
There's one more, the troublemaker.

251
00:19:30,712 --> 00:19:32,797
The four of them are a team.

252
00:19:32,881 --> 00:19:36,676
I know this might sound sexist
to people these days,

253
00:19:36,759 --> 00:19:40,930
but she causes more trouble than most men.

254
00:19:42,307 --> 00:19:44,392
A detective who's a woman?

255
00:19:44,475 --> 00:19:48,271
I feel like you'd be popular with women,

256
00:19:48,354 --> 00:19:49,981
given your looks.

257
00:19:50,064 --> 00:19:53,985
Women would line up for you
since you're a lawyer for Taekang, right?

258
00:19:54,068 --> 00:19:55,445
This guy was never popular.

259
00:19:55,528 --> 00:19:56,988
He joined a year later than me.

260
00:19:57,071 --> 00:19:59,407
Man, you're so handsome.

261
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:13,046
That feels better.

262
00:20:20,929 --> 00:20:22,430
-Yes, sir.
-Why aren't you here?

263
00:20:23,139 --> 00:20:24,974
Did you decide to run
before you got fired?

264
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:26,726
I'm on my way, sir.

265
00:20:26,809 --> 00:20:29,687
I'll give you ten minutes. You better run.

266
00:20:29,771 --> 00:20:31,481
I'll take more than--

267
00:20:32,523 --> 00:20:33,524
Hello?

268
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:38,404
Think.

269
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:40,114
All right.

270
00:20:41,991 --> 00:20:43,576
If he caught on that I'm a cop,

271
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:47,288
he would've asked Kim Si-hyun
so that he could sue me.

272
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:51,125
But what if he found out that I'm a woman?

273
00:20:51,209 --> 00:20:54,295
He would've asked Kim Si-hyun to fire me,
judging by his temper.

274
00:20:55,755 --> 00:20:58,716
But he's just agitated like always.

275
00:21:01,678 --> 00:21:03,554
I guess I didn't say much.

276
00:21:03,638 --> 00:21:05,765
Do you not remember anything?

277
00:21:05,848 --> 00:21:08,559
That could be a problem for you.

278
00:21:09,727 --> 00:21:11,771
This is a problem!

279
00:21:14,065 --> 00:21:16,109
Should I just bail? I should do that.

280
00:21:39,674 --> 00:21:40,591
Mr. Yoon.

281
00:21:41,926 --> 00:21:43,803
-Yesterday, I--
-I'm thinking about it.

282
00:21:43,886 --> 00:21:45,805
Whether to sue you through Kim Si-hyun

283
00:21:46,472 --> 00:21:48,099
or just fire you.

284
00:21:50,143 --> 00:21:52,603
I'm still deciding, so quietly wait.

285
00:21:56,858 --> 00:21:57,775
Ta-da.

286
00:21:58,651 --> 00:22:02,321
I bought this on the way
in case you don't feel well, sir.

287
00:22:04,198 --> 00:22:05,283
I see.

288
00:22:05,366 --> 00:22:07,243
My personal secretary bought me

289
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:10,747
a competitor's product on his way to work.

290
00:22:12,081 --> 00:22:13,958
Why is this…

291
00:22:16,127 --> 00:22:19,630
And it was even on
a buy-one-get-one-free deal?

292
00:22:19,714 --> 00:22:22,675
That wasn't my intention at all.

293
00:22:22,759 --> 00:22:24,927
You drank one for your hangover

294
00:22:25,011 --> 00:22:26,721
and acted like you bought this for me.

295
00:22:26,804 --> 00:22:28,890
That's not it. I figured

296
00:22:28,973 --> 00:22:30,516
you'd have a hangover like me,

297
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:34,145
so I saved one instead of drinking two.

298
00:22:34,228 --> 00:22:35,521
And I paid for it.

299
00:22:36,481 --> 00:22:40,151
That's how much I care about you,
Mr. Yoon.

300
00:22:44,947 --> 00:22:47,909
You don't remember last night,
you know I'm upset,

301
00:22:47,992 --> 00:22:51,871
and now you're trying to use flattery
to smooth things over?

302
00:22:51,954 --> 00:22:53,831
How is this flattery?

303
00:22:53,915 --> 00:22:58,127
You know how much I care about you.

304
00:22:59,420 --> 00:23:01,047
-Don't!
-What?

305
00:23:01,881 --> 00:23:03,299
Don't even think about me.

306
00:23:05,468 --> 00:23:07,720
I'm going to the office. Drive.

307
00:23:16,187 --> 00:23:18,815
Since he took the drink,
does that mean he's no longer upset?

308
00:23:31,744 --> 00:23:33,579
-Say it.
-It's okay, sir.

309
00:23:39,627 --> 00:23:40,753
About yesterday…

310
00:23:45,216 --> 00:23:46,634
Did Director Lee leave?

311
00:23:48,261 --> 00:23:50,763
Why do you care about Lee Si-a?

312
00:23:52,181 --> 00:23:54,767
She's absolutely gorgeous.

313
00:23:57,520 --> 00:24:00,148
Special Forces.
You're more ambitious than you look.

314
00:24:00,231 --> 00:24:01,190
Sir?

315
00:24:01,274 --> 00:24:04,318
It's understandable.
Lee Si-a is quite well off.

316
00:24:04,402 --> 00:24:07,280
Has that gotten your attention?

317
00:24:07,363 --> 00:24:08,239
What do you mean?

318
00:24:08,322 --> 00:24:11,075
I only asked because
you two looked great together.

319
00:24:11,159 --> 00:24:14,287
Of course, you could do better.

320
00:24:15,663 --> 00:24:17,665
-What?
-You're handsome,

321
00:24:17,748 --> 00:24:20,126
capable, and your personality is…

322
00:24:22,128 --> 00:24:25,381
You're a real man's man,
which is hard to see these days.

323
00:24:27,758 --> 00:24:29,302
I get it, so just drive.

324
00:24:29,385 --> 00:24:30,970
You're distracting me from work.

325
00:24:31,804 --> 00:24:33,139
Yes, sir.

326
00:24:48,321 --> 00:24:49,947
Don't get too close to me.

327
00:24:50,031 --> 00:24:51,032
I'm protecting you.

328
00:24:53,576 --> 00:24:55,661
Five steps back. No, ten.

329
00:24:55,745 --> 00:24:58,998
No, sir. It's my job to safely…

330
00:25:06,964 --> 00:25:09,467
Is this enough for ten steps?

331
00:25:09,550 --> 00:25:10,718
What are you doing?

332
00:25:11,302 --> 00:25:12,136
A little bit more?

333
00:25:15,973 --> 00:25:16,807
This much?

334
00:25:16,891 --> 00:25:18,309
How cute.

335
00:25:18,392 --> 00:25:19,685
I mean, no!

336
00:25:19,769 --> 00:25:20,603
Understood, sir.

337
00:25:27,068 --> 00:25:28,486
Mr. Yoon.

338
00:25:29,070 --> 00:25:29,904
Mr. Yoon!

339
00:25:31,989 --> 00:25:34,283
CHAIRMAN YOON TAE-SIK

340
00:25:36,619 --> 00:25:38,788
Managing Director Yoon came to work.

341
00:25:40,623 --> 00:25:43,626
I was surprised you withdrew
the share inheritance, sir.

342
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:46,671
I'm planning to observe
what they're up to.

343
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:48,547
Sir?

344
00:25:51,759 --> 00:25:54,428
There's no need
to push my children off the cliff.

345
00:25:54,512 --> 00:25:55,471
If I leave them be,

346
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:58,599
the strongest one
will win the prize anyway.

347
00:26:00,977 --> 00:26:01,811
Don't you agree?

348
00:26:05,064 --> 00:26:08,651
Director Lee Si-a went to see Mr. Yoon
as soon as she returned to Korea.

349
00:26:09,485 --> 00:26:11,320
I should meet Mr. Lee soon.

350
00:26:12,446 --> 00:26:13,906
I'll arrange it.

351
00:26:13,990 --> 00:26:17,618
With the election coming up, it would look
best to hold the wedding before then.

352
00:26:17,702 --> 00:26:19,036
Yes.

353
00:26:39,140 --> 00:26:41,767
The police were looking for the phone?

354
00:26:50,735 --> 00:26:54,071
Is there anything you need me to do
for the TF team, Hye-jung?

355
00:26:54,155 --> 00:26:55,364
I can take care of it.

356
00:26:56,324 --> 00:26:57,491
So you can see Mr. Kang?

357
00:26:57,575 --> 00:26:59,702
Yes, he's totally my type.

358
00:27:00,411 --> 00:27:02,705
I'd love to run into him in the cafeteria…

359
00:27:02,788 --> 00:27:03,789
What?

360
00:27:04,874 --> 00:27:06,459
Could I get one iced milk tea?

361
00:28:11,357 --> 00:28:13,609
Kim Si-hyun knows about the phone.
What happened?

362
00:28:14,193 --> 00:28:18,739
I don't know why he's being so suspicious.
He's sticking his nose into everything.

363
00:28:18,823 --> 00:28:22,034
He's sharp. He knows
we're going to search everywhere.

364
00:28:22,118 --> 00:28:24,578
We don't have much time.
We need to find the phone first.

365
00:28:24,662 --> 00:28:26,997
I traced Han Eun-young's steps
from her statement,

366
00:28:27,081 --> 00:28:28,499
but I found nothing.

367
00:28:28,582 --> 00:28:29,834
Honestly, the phone

368
00:28:29,917 --> 00:28:32,420
is even less likely to be here
than at Yoon's place.

369
00:28:32,503 --> 00:28:34,547
It's just that you can't find it.

370
00:28:34,630 --> 00:28:36,715
If that's how you're going to do it, quit.

371
00:28:36,799 --> 00:28:38,843
What do you even do there
while undercover?

372
00:28:38,926 --> 00:28:41,720
What do you even do
besides getting dishpan hands?

373
00:28:41,804 --> 00:28:44,432
Are you taking it out on me
after Kim Si-hyun gave you crap?

374
00:28:44,515 --> 00:28:45,599
Am I your punching bag?

375
00:28:45,683 --> 00:28:47,101
What did you say?

376
00:28:47,184 --> 00:28:48,352
Just wait.

377
00:28:48,436 --> 00:28:49,437
There's one place left.

378
00:28:50,229 --> 00:28:52,231
MATERIAL STORAGE

379
00:28:52,815 --> 00:28:53,899
I need to pick the lock.

380
00:28:55,609 --> 00:29:01,240
SIX DAYS AGO

381
00:29:01,323 --> 00:29:02,783
Goodness.

382
00:29:03,284 --> 00:29:05,327
You said you'd help,

383
00:29:05,411 --> 00:29:07,955
but it looks like you're wasting time.

384
00:29:08,539 --> 00:29:10,166
That desk is empty.

385
00:29:10,249 --> 00:29:12,793
They even replaced the desk
with a new one.

386
00:29:14,170 --> 00:29:16,505
-Replaced?
-Haven't you heard

387
00:29:16,964 --> 00:29:18,549
what happened to the owner?

388
00:29:18,632 --> 00:29:20,593
I've heard rumors.

389
00:29:21,469 --> 00:29:23,804
-But why would they replace it?
-Well…

390
00:29:24,180 --> 00:29:27,099
I guess it's for the new employee.

391
00:29:27,641 --> 00:29:29,810
No one even sits there,

392
00:29:29,894 --> 00:29:32,897
so I wonder who requested the replacement.

393
00:29:32,980 --> 00:29:36,817
You must've seen her working here.

394
00:29:36,901 --> 00:29:38,861
Who? The one who used to sit here?

395
00:29:38,944 --> 00:29:39,820
Yes.

396
00:29:41,155 --> 00:29:42,156
Oh dear.

397
00:29:42,239 --> 00:29:44,658
They say the old sayings never lie.

398
00:29:45,493 --> 00:29:48,120
They say people change
when they are about to die.

399
00:29:48,204 --> 00:29:49,955
And it was true for her too.

400
00:29:50,581 --> 00:29:53,000
Something must've weighed on her.

401
00:29:53,083 --> 00:29:55,252
She was mindlessly wandering around

402
00:29:55,336 --> 00:29:57,922
and saying things on the phone and stuff.

403
00:29:59,006 --> 00:30:00,591
I overheard her a bit…

404
00:30:00,674 --> 00:30:03,427
Yes. I checked everything.

405
00:30:04,386 --> 00:30:06,013
Mr. Yoon doesn't know yet.

406
00:30:07,973 --> 00:30:09,892
I know it's not my place to get involved.

407
00:30:10,518 --> 00:30:12,144
But it's too dangerous to ignore--

408
00:30:13,938 --> 00:30:14,855
…and

409
00:30:19,109 --> 00:30:22,738
I slipped out of the office because
I felt like I shouldn't be listening.

410
00:30:23,948 --> 00:30:27,993
Then a few days later,

411
00:30:28,702 --> 00:30:29,912
that happened.

412
00:30:31,664 --> 00:30:32,706
That poor thing.

413
00:30:44,426 --> 00:30:47,096
The replaced desk. The missing phone.

414
00:30:51,267 --> 00:30:52,601
Who was she on the phone with?

415
00:31:01,026 --> 00:31:03,320
It's fine. You may stay outside.

416
00:31:08,993 --> 00:31:12,079
Actually, go make my milk tea.

417
00:31:12,162 --> 00:31:13,956
-Make it refreshing.
-Yes, sir.

418
00:31:20,296 --> 00:31:21,922
This is an urgent matter.

419
00:31:22,006 --> 00:31:23,757
Have you lost your mind?

420
00:31:30,514 --> 00:31:31,348
Not me.

421
00:31:35,519 --> 00:31:37,771
How dare you

422
00:31:38,355 --> 00:31:40,357
add ice to my milk tea?

423
00:31:40,983 --> 00:31:42,568
You said you wanted it refreshing.

424
00:31:42,651 --> 00:31:44,445
So it's my fault?

425
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:46,363
Listen carefully.

426
00:31:46,447 --> 00:31:50,701
I'm very particular about every detail.

427
00:31:51,702 --> 00:31:52,995
Make it refreshing.

428
00:31:55,414 --> 00:31:59,168
Make it again with milk at exactly 58°C!

429
00:32:07,009 --> 00:32:10,054
Who told you to push
the 2 p.m. meeting back by 10 minutes?

430
00:32:10,137 --> 00:32:11,513
You, sir.

431
00:32:12,556 --> 00:32:14,558
You probably misheard me.

432
00:32:14,642 --> 00:32:16,935
Move it up five minutes. Now!

433
00:32:22,775 --> 00:32:23,984
What's wrong with him?

434
00:32:29,490 --> 00:32:33,202
Why does the 17-page concentration ratio
report only have 16 pages?

435
00:32:33,869 --> 00:32:35,537
You can't even copy it right?

436
00:32:36,205 --> 00:32:37,164
That report…

437
00:32:38,749 --> 00:32:42,002
You tore it apart during the meeting.

438
00:32:42,086 --> 00:32:43,295
Don't argue with me!

439
00:32:44,213 --> 00:32:45,047
Good grief.

440
00:32:46,256 --> 00:32:48,300
Whatever. Read it.

441
00:32:53,222 --> 00:32:54,139
My goodness.

442
00:32:56,392 --> 00:32:58,519
"Go do it again."

443
00:33:00,062 --> 00:33:01,105
"Again."

444
00:33:02,356 --> 00:33:03,524
Again!

445
00:33:13,242 --> 00:33:15,119
He's trying his best, sir.

446
00:33:15,869 --> 00:33:17,913
I think you could be a bit more forgiving.

447
00:33:22,126 --> 00:33:23,460
In other words,

448
00:33:23,544 --> 00:33:25,838
you're saying I'm being petty?

449
00:33:25,921 --> 00:33:29,967
-Therefore, I am being unreasonable?
-Yes.

450
00:33:31,510 --> 00:33:32,720
I mean, no.

451
00:33:32,803 --> 00:33:34,513
You're always generous, sir.

452
00:33:35,264 --> 00:33:39,226
It's all Secretary Kang's fault.
He's such a brat.

453
00:33:39,309 --> 00:33:43,564
Yes, I tried to forgive him
with an understanding heart.

454
00:33:43,647 --> 00:33:45,107
But he keeps…

455
00:33:45,190 --> 00:33:46,024
Yes, it's him.

456
00:33:46,108 --> 00:33:48,986
He's playing with my heart
with his weird words.

457
00:33:49,069 --> 00:33:52,656
That's how much I care about you,
Mr. Yoon.

458
00:33:52,740 --> 00:33:53,991
…how much I care about you.

459
00:33:54,074 --> 00:33:55,659
You're handsome,

460
00:33:55,743 --> 00:33:57,828
capable, and your personality is…

461
00:33:59,705 --> 00:34:03,083
You're a real man's man,
which is hard to see these days.

462
00:34:05,627 --> 00:34:07,588
Mr. Kang had it in him to do that?

463
00:34:08,630 --> 00:34:09,548
Get out.

464
00:34:18,015 --> 00:34:19,475
He's the one who tore it.

465
00:34:28,692 --> 00:34:30,194
Wee-woo, wee-woo.

466
00:34:41,413 --> 00:34:43,916
What was I looking for?

467
00:34:49,838 --> 00:34:52,674
It's a blind spot,
so watch for anyone nearby.

468
00:34:53,342 --> 00:34:54,510
What took you so long?

469
00:34:55,385 --> 00:34:58,180
Do you think a secretary
plays around all day?

470
00:34:59,389 --> 00:35:01,183
So? Is that it?

471
00:35:01,934 --> 00:35:04,144
Yes. What do you think the code is?

472
00:35:04,228 --> 00:35:05,771
Four zeros?

473
00:35:05,854 --> 00:35:09,775
How nice it would be
if everyone were a simpleton like you.

474
00:35:10,567 --> 00:35:11,401
It must be 1818.

475
00:35:11,485 --> 00:35:13,111
You're such a genius.

476
00:35:13,195 --> 00:35:15,030
You haven't tried it, right? Let's try.

477
00:35:15,614 --> 00:35:19,326
Don't open up about your feelings.
Open this door.

478
00:35:19,701 --> 00:35:22,287
I'll open that door in two days.

479
00:35:24,706 --> 00:35:28,085
Anyway, I heard Yoon Yi-jun
is giving you a hard time.

480
00:35:29,127 --> 00:35:32,172
Everyone is talking about
how bad they feel for you.

481
00:35:32,256 --> 00:35:33,173
Right?

482
00:35:33,674 --> 00:35:36,593
I deserve everyone's pity right now.

483
00:35:36,677 --> 00:35:38,554
His personality is so…

484
00:35:40,347 --> 00:35:41,640
damn awful.

485
00:35:42,599 --> 00:35:45,936
On the day you spammed
our group chat while drunk,

486
00:35:47,771 --> 00:35:49,523
you did something to Yoon Yi-jun, right?

487
00:35:53,235 --> 00:35:54,152
No.

488
00:35:57,030 --> 00:35:59,116
Handcuffs? Are you crazy?

489
00:36:00,784 --> 00:36:02,619
Are you serious? Are you kidding?

490
00:36:02,703 --> 00:36:05,706
Are you for real? Are you crazy?

491
00:36:08,041 --> 00:36:09,877
Don't tell the captain.

492
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:11,879
I'll take care of it soon.

493
00:36:11,962 --> 00:36:12,796
No wonder.

494
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:16,466
I knew something was off
when you let him push you around.

495
00:36:17,301 --> 00:36:18,552
What if he caught on?

496
00:36:19,511 --> 00:36:20,762
I don't think he did.

497
00:36:20,846 --> 00:36:22,723
If he knew about our undercover operation,

498
00:36:22,806 --> 00:36:24,516
I would not be sitting here.

499
00:36:24,600 --> 00:36:26,184
Actually, our whole team…

500
00:36:26,768 --> 00:36:29,146
No, he'll destroy the whole policy agency.

501
00:36:29,229 --> 00:36:32,357
So why on earth is he giving you
such a hard time?

502
00:36:33,150 --> 00:36:37,070
I remember running around
to chase the cat.

503
00:36:37,154 --> 00:36:38,405
Are you crazy?

504
00:36:39,948 --> 00:36:41,491
Don't you know our captain?

505
00:36:41,575 --> 00:36:43,368
The captain is going to give us hell.

506
00:36:43,452 --> 00:36:44,536
I know.

507
00:36:45,579 --> 00:36:49,374
I'll buy some time
until you can get that door open.

508
00:36:49,791 --> 00:36:51,293
You better remember what happened.

509
00:36:51,376 --> 00:36:53,045
-Okay?
-Yes.

510
00:36:56,882 --> 00:36:57,799
You've heard, right?

511
00:37:00,469 --> 00:37:02,596
The meeting between Kim Si-hyun
and Yoon Na-jung.

512
00:37:03,096 --> 00:37:06,350
It does seem a bit suspicious
since she tried to recruit me too.

513
00:37:06,433 --> 00:37:09,603
But Kim Si-hyun and Yoon Yi-jun
have been friends since high school.

514
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:13,523
So? You think money won't come
between lifelong friends?

515
00:37:14,983 --> 00:37:16,818
Also, from what I hear,

516
00:37:17,527 --> 00:37:19,363
Kim Si-hyun tipped Yoon Na-jung off

517
00:37:19,446 --> 00:37:24,076
about the progress
of Taekang's succession plan.

518
00:37:24,159 --> 00:37:25,786
That two-faced bastard.

519
00:37:27,371 --> 00:37:31,625
Anyway, Yoon Na-jung and Yoon Yi-jun
are fighting it out behind the scenes.

520
00:37:32,501 --> 00:37:34,544
But even Chairman Yoon's right-hand man,

521
00:37:35,087 --> 00:37:37,923
the chief secretary,
has been acting suspiciously lately.

522
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:40,801
It's been a while.

523
00:37:43,512 --> 00:37:45,013
It's been a while, everyone.

524
00:37:45,597 --> 00:37:47,224
Have you all been well?

525
00:37:47,307 --> 00:37:48,350
It's been a while.

526
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:53,814
These are our journalists.

527
00:37:53,897 --> 00:37:55,691
-Hello.
-Hello.

528
00:37:55,774 --> 00:37:58,443
It's a good day. Let's be on the same page

529
00:37:59,152 --> 00:38:00,779
and write some warm stories.

530
00:38:00,862 --> 00:38:02,364
-Yes.
-I look forward to them.

531
00:38:02,447 --> 00:38:03,740
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

532
00:38:04,449 --> 00:38:06,284
You all know what you need to do, right?

533
00:38:06,368 --> 00:38:07,327
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

534
00:38:09,287 --> 00:38:10,414
You're here, Na-jung.

535
00:38:11,081 --> 00:38:12,958
Welcome. Thank you for coming.

536
00:38:14,668 --> 00:38:16,545
-Hello, Jun-hyun.
-Hello.

537
00:38:17,462 --> 00:38:18,839
The second child, Yoon Na-jung,

538
00:38:18,922 --> 00:38:20,757
has quite a notorious reputation.

539
00:38:21,842 --> 00:38:23,719
Apparently, she's downright nasty.

540
00:38:24,302 --> 00:38:26,179
I saw her at the family meeting.

541
00:38:26,263 --> 00:38:29,057
Yoon Na-jung
absolutely loathes Yoon Yi-jun.

542
00:38:30,976 --> 00:38:32,394
What about the eldest?

543
00:38:32,477 --> 00:38:33,687
Yoon Mi-jin?

544
00:38:34,646 --> 00:38:35,856
Of the three siblings,

545
00:38:35,939 --> 00:38:38,942
she's the most like her father
in business.

546
00:38:39,026 --> 00:38:40,527
I heard she's a good person.

547
00:38:40,610 --> 00:38:43,155
She's supportive of Yoon Yi-jun
and isn't so ambitious.

548
00:38:44,156 --> 00:38:47,492
If it's over succession,
is she on good terms with the others?

549
00:38:48,035 --> 00:38:49,119
The chief secretary?

550
00:38:49,202 --> 00:38:50,829
They're his late sister's kids,

551
00:38:50,912 --> 00:38:52,831
so he's a good uncle to them, I guess.

552
00:39:11,433 --> 00:39:14,394
Please smile bigger. Thank you.

553
00:39:14,478 --> 00:39:17,105
One, two, three.

554
00:39:17,189 --> 00:39:18,732
-We can do it!
-We can do it!

555
00:39:22,027 --> 00:39:23,820
One more shot.

556
00:39:23,904 --> 00:39:26,114
One, two, three.

557
00:39:26,198 --> 00:39:27,991
Thank you for coming to support us

558
00:39:28,784 --> 00:39:30,494
despite being so busy, Ms. Yoon.

559
00:39:31,078 --> 00:39:34,039
Taekang Cultural Foundation is
a VIP of our hotel's catering service.

560
00:39:34,122 --> 00:39:35,415
Of course I should come.

561
00:39:36,958 --> 00:39:38,835
-Let's do a heart pose this time.
-Sure.

562
00:39:39,628 --> 00:39:41,963
It's supposed to be a Taekang event,

563
00:39:42,047 --> 00:39:43,423
but it's a bit drab.

564
00:39:43,965 --> 00:39:45,717
Host it at our hotel starting next year.

565
00:39:47,427 --> 00:39:48,345
What?

566
00:39:48,887 --> 00:39:50,305
Or maybe it's not a good idea.

567
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:52,224
A project for ex-cons

568
00:39:52,307 --> 00:39:54,434
doesn't really fit the hotel's image.

569
00:39:58,021 --> 00:40:00,232
I put a lot of effort into this event.

570
00:40:00,315 --> 00:40:01,983
I hope you'll support us generously.

571
00:40:02,067 --> 00:40:05,946
Ever since Father put you
in charge of the foundation,

572
00:40:06,029 --> 00:40:07,906
this has been the only event
that's thrived.

573
00:40:08,740 --> 00:40:10,408
Of course, I'll lend my support.

574
00:40:13,036 --> 00:40:15,580
I'll let the chairman know
that you came today.

575
00:40:15,664 --> 00:40:17,833
You don't have to go that far.

576
00:40:17,916 --> 00:40:19,668
I can take care of myself.

577
00:40:21,586 --> 00:40:24,047
Why do you think
I brought those journalists with me?

578
00:40:25,841 --> 00:40:28,468
We need to get some photos
of them smiling.

579
00:40:29,261 --> 00:40:30,387
In high school,

580
00:40:30,470 --> 00:40:34,099
there was this brat who always kept me
from being the top student.

581
00:40:35,475 --> 00:40:36,977
Do you know what I did to her?

582
00:40:38,436 --> 00:40:40,939
Seeing your personality,

583
00:40:41,606 --> 00:40:43,441
you probably tried harder.

584
00:40:43,525 --> 00:40:44,693
Of course.

585
00:40:45,569 --> 00:40:47,320
I drugged her lunch.

586
00:40:51,825 --> 00:40:55,036
Father complimented me
that day for the first time.

587
00:40:55,120 --> 00:40:56,079
That's when I realized

588
00:40:56,955 --> 00:40:58,915
that I should take what I wanted,

589
00:41:00,250 --> 00:41:02,002
by any means necessary,

590
00:41:03,378 --> 00:41:04,337
all on my own.

591
00:41:16,349 --> 00:41:17,225
Park Min-hwan.

592
00:41:18,935 --> 00:41:19,853
Where is he?

593
00:41:24,024 --> 00:41:25,984
If what he ran off with gets out,

594
00:41:26,526 --> 00:41:29,154
a lot of people won't be happy.

595
00:41:30,197 --> 00:41:31,198
I'm curious.

596
00:41:32,574 --> 00:41:36,161
Would you be one of them,
Executive Director Yoon?

597
00:41:46,880 --> 00:41:49,883
I mean, I'm pretty good
at figuring people out.

598
00:41:50,717 --> 00:41:52,427
But you're a tricky one.

599
00:41:55,263 --> 00:41:58,058
Are you on the chairman's side,
Yoon Yi-jun's side,

600
00:41:58,850 --> 00:41:59,935
or my side?

601
00:42:03,313 --> 00:42:04,648
Make it clear now.

602
00:42:10,946 --> 00:42:13,281
Bring Park Min-hwan to me,

603
00:42:15,784 --> 00:42:17,827
and I'll tell you what you want to know.

604
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:25,252
I'm not a philanthropist.

605
00:42:55,198 --> 00:42:57,534
Secretary Han had two phones?

606
00:42:57,617 --> 00:42:59,786
Why are the police looking for it?

607
00:42:59,869 --> 00:43:01,746
They think something is on the phone.

608
00:43:02,414 --> 00:43:03,790
Where could it be?

609
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:06,668
What if someone took it?

610
00:43:07,544 --> 00:43:09,254
Are you afraid someone else will die?

611
00:43:11,131 --> 00:43:12,757
Should you be worrying about others?

612
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:24,769
I have to do everything I can
to prevent further harm.

613
00:43:25,520 --> 00:43:27,147
Right, about Manager Park…

614
00:43:29,941 --> 00:43:31,192
Is he in a safe place?

615
00:43:36,573 --> 00:43:37,615
Seok-jin.

616
00:43:37,699 --> 00:43:41,161
Can you find out
where the herbicide in the milk is from?

617
00:43:41,244 --> 00:43:43,955
This thing can kill anything,
animals or plants.

618
00:43:52,881 --> 00:43:54,466
BUSINESS REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE

619
00:44:10,148 --> 00:44:13,193
Everything only has real value

620
00:44:13,735 --> 00:44:15,904
when it finds the right owner.

621
00:44:25,121 --> 00:44:26,831
It's hard to read.

622
00:44:26,915 --> 00:44:29,376
Do it again! Again!

623
00:44:33,254 --> 00:44:35,590
He's like Cinderella's wicked stepmother.

624
00:44:43,598 --> 00:44:45,642
This isn't what I'm here for.

625
00:45:00,240 --> 00:45:01,616
Gosh. What?

626
00:45:02,409 --> 00:45:04,369
Why? What happened?

627
00:45:04,452 --> 00:45:08,540
The desk suddenly collapsed,
and this happened.

628
00:45:10,041 --> 00:45:11,334
Hold on.

629
00:45:12,168 --> 00:45:13,002
What?

630
00:45:14,421 --> 00:45:15,922
The desk is causing trouble now?

631
00:45:18,425 --> 00:45:19,300
What do we do?

632
00:45:23,638 --> 00:45:25,473
Open the link and request a replacement.

633
00:45:26,391 --> 00:45:27,642
They'll reach out to you.

634
00:45:28,435 --> 00:45:29,352
Thank you.

635
00:45:37,527 --> 00:45:38,403
DESK CHANGE

636
00:45:39,154 --> 00:45:40,029
What?

637
00:45:40,113 --> 00:45:42,615
Someone requested to replace a desk?

638
00:45:44,409 --> 00:45:45,452
Who could it be?

639
00:45:46,536 --> 00:45:48,079
SEOK-JIN

640
00:45:59,549 --> 00:46:00,383
Hey.

641
00:46:00,467 --> 00:46:02,135
Have you heard of Bowoon Chemical?

642
00:46:02,218 --> 00:46:03,761
Bowoon Chemical?

643
00:46:03,845 --> 00:46:06,139
They're the sole importer
of herbicide ingredients

644
00:46:06,222 --> 00:46:08,183
and one of Taekang Chemical's
subsidiaries.

645
00:46:08,266 --> 00:46:09,434
Yoon Na-jung runs

646
00:46:10,393 --> 00:46:12,479
Taekang Hotels and Taekang Chemical.

647
00:46:16,065 --> 00:46:17,108
Yoon Na-jung?

648
00:46:37,670 --> 00:46:38,838
Are you afraid

649
00:46:41,090 --> 00:46:42,258
someone else will die?

650
00:47:11,788 --> 00:47:15,708
The herbicide from Taekang Chemical,
run by Executive Director Yoon Na-jung,

651
00:47:17,252 --> 00:47:19,796
the milk delivered
by Attorney Kim Si-hyun,

652
00:47:20,922 --> 00:47:24,968
Yoon Na-jung and Kim Si-hyun
meeting late at night…

653
00:47:26,678 --> 00:47:27,637
Kim Si-hyun.

654
00:47:49,367 --> 00:47:50,868
Are you okay, sir?

655
00:48:11,848 --> 00:48:13,433
Was I just treated like an intruder?

656
00:48:13,516 --> 00:48:15,643
I apologize for my rudeness.
Please forgive me.

657
00:48:22,692 --> 00:48:24,652
I really like you, Secretary Kang.

658
00:48:26,321 --> 00:48:28,031
You keep getting more interesting.

659
00:48:32,327 --> 00:48:33,578
Can I have your number?

660
00:48:35,079 --> 00:48:35,913
Yi-jun.

661
00:48:39,834 --> 00:48:40,710
Give it to her.

662
00:48:46,924 --> 00:48:49,302
I want to call you every day. Can I?

663
00:48:49,385 --> 00:48:51,346
-No.
-You can if you want.

664
00:48:54,223 --> 00:48:57,018
Since you guys don't agree on it,
I'll do what I want.

665
00:49:00,813 --> 00:49:03,358
Go play with Jerry.
You two need to get close, right?

666
00:49:04,942 --> 00:49:06,944
Let's go out. I thought you wanted to eat.

667
00:49:07,612 --> 00:49:09,656
Yes, I want some meat.

668
00:49:09,739 --> 00:49:11,115
Nice and bloody.

669
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:13,743
I like it rare.

670
00:49:18,414 --> 00:49:19,332
What did he say?

671
00:49:19,415 --> 00:49:21,793
Did he tell you to quit?
Is he going to fire you?

672
00:49:22,335 --> 00:49:24,170
No, I don't think so.

673
00:49:24,253 --> 00:49:26,422
Of all people,
you didn't recognize his fiancée.

674
00:49:27,924 --> 00:49:29,217
Wait here.

675
00:49:29,300 --> 00:49:31,344
I'll take responsibility and beg him

676
00:49:31,427 --> 00:49:33,012
to let me retrain you.

677
00:49:39,394 --> 00:49:40,770
You stay.

678
00:49:41,354 --> 00:49:42,313
Don't follow us.

679
00:49:49,904 --> 00:49:52,615
Let's be friends. I'll call you.

680
00:49:56,744 --> 00:49:58,413
You must be shaken. Go home for today.

681
00:49:58,496 --> 00:49:59,872
I'll follow him for today.

682
00:50:06,838 --> 00:50:09,132
I haven't had
a dopamine rush like this in ages.

683
00:50:12,552 --> 00:50:14,554
Things will get interesting from now on.

684
00:50:25,481 --> 00:50:27,692
You stay. Don't follow us.

685
00:50:30,445 --> 00:50:32,989
-Did you ask for a replacement?
-Yes, this one.

686
00:50:41,789 --> 00:50:43,624
-Thank you.
-Thanks.

687
00:51:00,433 --> 00:51:01,768
They just took the desk.

688
00:51:02,268 --> 00:51:03,936
Okay.

689
00:51:09,984 --> 00:51:11,486
Gosh, hello.

690
00:51:12,320 --> 00:51:15,114
It looks like it's been a while
since this room was cleaned.

691
00:51:15,198 --> 00:51:17,992
Since I'm here, I'll just clean the floor.

692
00:51:18,409 --> 00:51:19,744
Sure, go ahead.

693
00:51:20,703 --> 00:51:22,246
Close the door properly afterward.

694
00:51:22,330 --> 00:51:23,539
Of course.

695
00:51:23,623 --> 00:51:24,874
-Thank you.
-Thanks.

696
00:51:34,300 --> 00:51:35,218
-Bin.
-Bin.

697
00:51:37,845 --> 00:51:40,097
Bin! Hurry up and come here!

698
00:51:41,474 --> 00:51:43,518
Yes, I'll be there soon.

699
00:51:56,405 --> 00:51:57,281
Okay.

700
00:52:11,796 --> 00:52:12,672
Let's see.

701
00:52:15,883 --> 00:52:17,885
The product number

702
00:52:17,969 --> 00:52:21,931
is 807TKKSOZ398.

703
00:52:27,019 --> 00:52:29,814
EQUIPMENT REPLACEMENT APPLICATION
REQUESTED BY: LEE HYE-JUNG

704
00:52:29,897 --> 00:52:31,023
Lee Hye-jung?

705
00:52:53,170 --> 00:52:54,088
Aren't you hungry?

706
00:52:56,883 --> 00:52:57,884
Because I am.

707
00:53:10,563 --> 00:53:11,397
Let's see.

708
00:53:26,412 --> 00:53:27,246
What?

709
00:53:32,460 --> 00:53:33,502
I don't see anything.

710
00:54:05,326 --> 00:54:06,160
Yi-jun.

711
00:54:07,662 --> 00:54:09,872
You'll go to hell

712
00:54:10,665 --> 00:54:11,999
if you waste food.

713
00:54:13,709 --> 00:54:15,044
Let's just go quietly.

714
00:54:18,965 --> 00:54:22,677
You look absolutely miserable,
like you haven't seen the sun in ages.

715
00:54:23,260 --> 00:54:24,929
Speaking of which,

716
00:54:26,013 --> 00:54:27,264
I want to get married.

717
00:54:28,224 --> 00:54:31,060
As soon as possible.
The timing is right too.

718
00:54:33,062 --> 00:54:35,856
So this time, Yoon Yi-jun,
I need you to cooperate.

719
00:54:37,858 --> 00:54:42,321
Pick whatever announcement date you want,
before or after the shareholder meeting.

720
00:54:43,114 --> 00:54:44,490
Whatever works in your favor.

721
00:54:55,876 --> 00:54:58,295
Did Special Forces have dinner?

722
00:54:58,921 --> 00:54:59,755
Sir?

723
00:55:02,508 --> 00:55:05,011
Did you make sure he had dinner?

724
00:55:05,594 --> 00:55:07,054
I made sure he had dinner.

725
00:55:07,888 --> 00:55:10,057
And I had instant noodles while waiting.

726
00:55:12,018 --> 00:55:13,019
Okay.

727
00:55:47,136 --> 00:55:49,513
I hope we can find something.

728
00:55:49,597 --> 00:55:52,224
The captain is going to
give it to forensics, so let's wait.

729
00:55:52,308 --> 00:55:55,519
I'm getting out of here
as soon as we catch the culprit.

730
00:55:56,395 --> 00:55:58,189
I heard he's giving you a hard time.

731
00:55:59,023 --> 00:56:01,067
Do you know how cruel he is?

732
00:56:01,150 --> 00:56:05,071
I look out for him,
but he just tells me to get out.

733
00:56:06,947 --> 00:56:10,117
But when you think about it, I'm worse.

734
00:56:10,993 --> 00:56:12,661
I'll have to betray him in the end.

735
00:56:14,330 --> 00:56:17,083
Once Yoon Yi-jun finds out
who I really am,

736
00:56:17,875 --> 00:56:19,418
he'll feel betrayed.

737
00:56:26,258 --> 00:56:27,093
Kang Jae-hee!

738
00:56:30,096 --> 00:56:32,306
You should go now, Seok-jin.

739
00:56:43,734 --> 00:56:46,112
Didn't you say you were going to dinner?

740
00:56:50,407 --> 00:56:53,452
I need to check something with you.

741
00:56:54,495 --> 00:56:55,329
What?

742
00:56:56,747 --> 00:56:58,207
You started it.

743
00:57:21,105 --> 00:57:23,190
You protected me.

744
00:57:23,274 --> 00:57:26,735
Why do you keep
seeing things I don't want you to see?

745
00:58:36,805 --> 00:58:38,682
SPECIAL THANKS TO
CHOI HEE-JIN AND JUNG YOO-MIN

746
00:58:38,766 --> 00:58:42,061
Why does everyone like Mr. Kang?
Never mind. You like him too, right?

747
00:58:42,937 --> 00:58:43,979
Get out!

748
00:58:44,063 --> 00:58:46,857
He'll win the election. Announce the
wedding before the shareholder meeting.

749
00:58:46,941 --> 00:58:49,443
He's Yi-jun's new secretary.
Give him to me.

750
00:58:49,526 --> 00:58:53,030
It didn't make sense. I shouldn't
have been confused to begin with.

751
00:58:53,113 --> 00:58:56,450
There's a weird rumor
about Attorney Kim and Ms. Yoon Na-jung.

752
00:58:56,533 --> 00:58:58,786
I approached you intentionally,
Attorney Kim.

753
00:58:58,869 --> 00:59:00,579
Mr. Kang, you always act independently.

754
00:59:00,663 --> 00:59:02,039
Is it just me who finds it odd?

755
00:59:02,122 --> 00:59:05,000
-Just do what you're told!
-I was mistaken for a moment.

756
00:59:05,084 --> 00:59:06,835
I thought maybe you were a good person.

757
00:59:07,461 --> 00:59:10,464
Translated by Leo Chung
